Subject: Cantor Identity Accounting MCP Durable Store P2 Justification

& [Decision]
  + immutable content-addressed whole-journal snapshots avoid platform-specific replace semantics and leave crash recovery evidence inspectable
  + unique maximal prefix recovery rejects split-brain histories instead of guessing which file is latest
  + persist-before-publish makes a successful mutation response evidence of locally synced snapshot custody
  + one mutex makes the core compare-and-set root effective across concurrent MCP calls
  + a separate crate contains filesystem authority so cantor_core remains pure

& [Rejected]
  + overwriting one mutable file because Windows replacement semantics and crash windows obscure prior good state
  + choosing by modification time because wall-clock metadata is not semantic lineage
  + deleting old generations because P2 is custody not retention policy
  + silently selecting one fork because ambiguity must remain visible
